From b7344025e05ca465be7c28d4d3b8e2de67473179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:53:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] unloaded host lease: beat after a raising pass,
 holder capacity only for a real lease, one notice-fanout connection

Follow-up to PR #2169 (review 5891002989 nits, card t_01a1d4e38cf61e24).

1. kanban_unloaded.run_pass beats in a finally, as producer_admission.run_pass does. A host pass that raised
   (card_change_pass, guarantee_pass) skipped beat(), so the watchdog dropped the lease after 3x interval and a
   live .want hand-off waited for that drop instead of the next pass end.
2. HostLoopLease.exclusive(): True only while this process really holds the flock (False under the kill switch
   and when the lease failed open). run_pass sizes wake slots on it instead of held() and the env switch alone:
   a failed-open lease (no fcntl, no usable lock) made held() True in every process, so each got the holder's
   8 wake slots instead of the pre-lease 2.
3. notice_fanout_state keeps one connection per (path, pid), opened (PRAGMA journal_mode + schema) once; a
   failed statement drops it so the next call reopens. Before, every get/set opened a connection and reran both:
   12 connects for one 3-board pass in the new test, now 1.
4. Without a real lease (HERMES_HOST_LOOP_LEASE=0, or failed open) host_pass retries killed-subagent notices in
   this process's own store (server._get_db(), as before #2169) instead of every profile store, so the kill
   switch is an exact rollback. The real holder still retries every store.

Tests (tests/tui_gateway/test_kanban_unloaded_host_lease.py), RED on origin/main 1b889c6115 (6 failed: kill-switch
and fail-open own-store retry, beat on raise, fail-open base slots, real-holder exclusive(), connection count
12 != 1), GREEN here. All 31 test files importing kanban_unloaded / notice_fanout / host_loop_lease /
wake_slots / reap_notices / producer_admission: 422 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
